assets_used = PackedStringArray("Female_Alternative", "Female_Casual", "Female_Dress", "Female_TankTop", "Smooth_Female_Alternative", "Smooth_Female_Casual", "Smooth_Female_Dress", "Smooth_Female_TankTop")
per_file_licensing = false
notes = "CC0 — crediting is courtesy, not compliance. Separate entry from
quaternius_animated_men_characters.tres because it is a separate pack download with its
own License.txt on disk, even though the two texts are identical and the two packs share
one rig; merging them would make the entry stop matching what a reviewer finds in
source-content/assets/.

license_file is this pack's OWN License.txt, copied verbatim from
source-content/assets/Animated Women Characters - Feb 2019.../License.txt, not the shared
generic Quaternius CC0 boilerplate.

All 8 models ship the same HumanArmature rig (42 bones) and the same 11 clips
(HumanArmature|Female_Clapping/Death/Idle/Jump/Punch/Run/RunningJump/Sitting/Standing/
SwordSlash/Walk) — measured on import, not assumed. The four Smooth_* models are
subdivided twins of the four base models: identical silhouette and identical material
set, roughly 3.5-4x the triangles. Both sets were imported on purpose so the base-vs-
smooth comparison can be made in-engine; whichever set loses gets pulled later.

DISTINCT FROM the AnimatedWoman model recorded in
quaternius_poly_pizza_characters.tres — that one is a different, later Quaternius release
on the CharacterArmature rig (24 clips) and is NOT from this pack. Nothing was moved
between those entries; only Man was (see the men's entry for that correction)."
